IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-provisions`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), s 5: determinative and non-determinative provisions.
--
-- A determinative provision is a provision of this Act that is declared to be a determinative provision (s 5 (2)).
-- A non-determinative provision is any other provision of this Act (s 5 (3)).
-- This module holds one constant for each sentence of the in-scope text that declares a provision determinative,
-- written by a script that reads the text file, and the rule of s 5 over them.
-- A section outside the in-scope text has no entry here, so the rule answers NOTHING for it.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): determinative provisions`

DECLARE `How far a provision is declared determinative` IS ONE OF
    `entirely`
    `so far as it applies to an applicable law or applicable provision`

DECLARE `Declaration of determinative status` HAS
    `section` IS A STRING
    `how far` IS A `How far a provision is declared determinative`

DECLARE `Determinative status` IS ONE OF
    `a determinative provision`
    `a determinative provision so far as it applies to an applicable law or applicable provision`
    `a non-determinative provision`

-- src:106 | (3) This section is a determinative provision.
@ref s 4 (3) (src:106-106)
GIVETH A `Declaration of determinative status`
`s 4 (3): the section declares itself a determinative provision` MEANS
    `Declaration of determinative status` WITH `section` IS "4", `how far` IS `entirely`

